      {
        "number": 7,
        "page": 4,
        "marks": 3,
        "stem": "In the given diagram, one end of a string is attached to a tuning fork with frequency 120 Hz, while the other end of the string passes over a frictionless pulley and is connected to a suspended mass $M$. The value of $M$ is such that the standing wave pattern has four loops. The length of the string from the tuning fork to the point where the string touches the top of the pulley is 2.0 m.\na. Determine the wavelength of the standing wave. (1 Mark)\nb. Determine the speed of transverse waves along the string. (1 Mark)\nc. Explain the effect of increasing the number of loops on velocity and frequency of the standing waves. (1 Mark)",
        "choices": {},
