      {
        "number": 10,
        "page": 7,
        "marks": 7,
        "stem": "EITHER\na.\nTwo containers (A) and (B) are placed at a high-temperature reservoir. Container (A) is at constant volume ($C_v$) and container (B) is at constant pressure ($C_p$). Show that the heat capacity at constant pressure ($C_p$) is greater than that of heat capacity at constant volume ($C_v$).\nOR\nb.\nAn inventor looking for financial support approaches you with an idea of an engine that runs on a unique type of thermodynamic cycle. His design is made entirely of copper and is air-cooled. He claims that the engine will be 88% efficient. Whereas the melting point of copper is 1083°C and the exhaust temperature is 27°C.\nShould you invest in this new engine? Why or why not? Justify your answer using calculations.",
